The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
ret = ida_simple_get(&nhi->msix_ida, 0, MSIX_MAX_VECS, GFP_KERNEL);
if (ret < 0)
    return ret;
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because when `ida_simple_get()` successfully allocates an IDA entry but an error occurs later in the function (either during IRQ vector retrieval or IRQ request), the function does not call `ida_simple_remove()`. This omission leads to a resource leak, as the allocated IDA entry remains in use without being properly cleaned up.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (ret < 0)
    goto err_ida_remove;
...
err_ida_remove:
    ida_simple_remove(&nhi->msix_ida, ring->vector);
```
Reason:
The fix introduces an error handling path that jumps to the `err_ida_remove` label when an error occurs after successfully allocating an IDA entry. This ensures that `ida_simple_remove()` is called to properly clean up the IDA entry, preventing resource leaks and maintaining consistent state management.

